## 12. Reliability and AI Validation

- Use structured output where supported.
- Validate LLM responses using Pydantic.
- Retry malformed outputs in a controlled manner.
- Prevent fabricated requirement IDs.
- Validate every source reference against the approved URS.
- Prevent duplicate test case IDs.
- Keep confidence and assumptions visible.
- Log generation errors safely.
- Handle API rate limits and timeouts.

Do not let the LLM determine actual execution results.

A generated test case is not a passed test case.

